{"4673750": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Country Town Trains", "steam_appid": 4673750, "required_age": 0, "is_free": true, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome To Country Town Trains</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Intro:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a casual train simulation game. Anyone can play. This game has no story, or accomplishments. This is a cozy game especially for train lovers and Railfans. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >How To Play:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use the mouse, keyboard, or Xbox styled controller. Choose your desired mode, and play. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game Content:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game features Town mode. When you play in Town Mode, you sit back, relax and watch the trains pass by, just like in a small town.  Note, the content of this game is 2D only.  Sit back and watch the trains pass through the small town. You will not receive any reward for watching the trains pass. Town mode play is strictly casual, adventurous, making for a cozy experience. More modes may be added in the future. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Derailments:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Derailments are not supported now, but stay posted for updates. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Translation:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is going to be made in at least English. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Contrast:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game switches to a lighter theme during the day, and switches to a darker theme at night. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Credit:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game was proudly manufactured in White Castle, Louisiana. This game was made in singularity by just 1 biracial light skinned autistic man. This game was not made with a game engine, but was made in pure c++, with skill. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Train Image Assets:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The image assets used in this game was made by a autistic biracial light skinned man, and belongs to a autistic biracial light skinned man. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Data Safety:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This software does not include any network libraries in the source code. No intrusive technology such as cookies are in this game. This game is safe to play, no strings attached. Your data will not be used to train the so called &quot;artificial intelligence&quot; models. This game is entirely offline. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This software is highly optimized. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*NOTE: This game has not been tested or developed for 4K displays or higher. If you have a 4K monitor, you will need to change your resolution to at least 1080p to play. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome To Country Town Trains</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Intro:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a casual train simulation game. Anyone can play. This game has no story, or accomplishments. This is a cozy game especially for train lovers and Railfans. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >How To Play:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use the mouse, keyboard, or Xbox styled controller. Choose your desired mode, and play. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Game Content:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game features Town mode. When you play in Town Mode, you sit back, relax and watch the trains pass by, just like in a small town.  Note, the content of this game is 2D only.  Sit back and watch the trains pass through the small town. You will not receive any reward for watching the trains pass. Town mode play is strictly casual, adventurous, making for a cozy experience. More modes may be added in the future. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Derailments:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Derailments are not supported now, but stay posted for updates. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Translation:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game is going to be made in at least English. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Contrast:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game switches to a lighter theme during the day, and switches to a darker theme at night. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Credit:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game was proudly manufactured in White Castle, Louisiana. This game was made in singularity by just 1 biracial light skinned autistic man. This game was not made with a game engine, but was made in pure c++, with skill. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Train Image Assets:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The image assets used in this game was made by a autistic biracial light skinned man, and belongs to a autistic biracial light skinned man. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Data Safety:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This software does not include any network libraries in the source code. No intrusive technology such as cookies are in this game. This game is safe to play, no strings attached. Your data will not be used to train the so called &quot;artificial intelligence&quot; models. This game is entirely offline. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This software is highly optimized. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*NOTE: This game has not been tested or developed for 4K displays or higher. If you have a 4K monitor, you will need to change your resolution to at least 1080p to play. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "Connect With Nature As You Railfan! Stargaze, Moongaze, Snow Gaze, whatever you want! Choose how many train cars and the terrain type! Uphill, Downhill, Flat. Realistic hill degrees and realistic load capacity calculations. Made in White Castle, Louisiana, each locomotive wears that with pride.", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4673750/9733bc3ffa9832b149e31199fee8483b6a57568b/header.jpg?t=1788016791", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4673750/6efba452d2252670c6a3f5505a38d8e4ad6a3bad/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1788016791", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4673750/6efba452d2252670c6a3f5505a38d8e4ad6a3bad/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1788016791", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong>  Windows 7 / 8 / 10 / 11 (64-bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> 1.0 GHz Single Core (Intel Pentium 4 / AMD Athlon)<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4096 MB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> OpenGL 2.0 (No Dedicated Card Needed) Anything From 2005+<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 10<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 6 MB available space</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 /11 (64-bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> 2.0 GHz Dual Core<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4096 MB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> OpenGL 2.0 (No Dedicated Card Needed) Anything From 2005+<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 6 MB available space</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": {"mini